    "created_at": "2026-06-04T18:16:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-04T18:16:06Z",
    "body": "I would really like to see this approach used instead of cloning for customizable select, even removing cloning before customizable select ships cross-browser.\n\nCloning just doesn't work in general. It doesn't support non-markup state (JS properties, input value, select selected item, etc.) and it can massively interfere with code that introspects the DOM on startup, like SSR hydration (see https://github.com/lit/lit/issues/5349), which will process the cloned contents of `<selectionoption>` as if they were server-rendered.\n\nMirroring fixes these problems, even if it does have complexities like mentioned in https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9284",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
